### Outline rail — `sz-toc`

A sticky outline (scroll-spy: highlights the current section, click to jump) plus a thin top progress bar. It reads headings straight from the rendered page, so it needs no data — auto-injected above every article body; drop `<sz-toc>` to add it elsewhere.

<sz-toc></sz-toc>

### Liquid glass — `sz-glass`

A material, not a widget: it renders a refractive, tinted, specular-lit surface behind its slot and knows nothing about what it wraps. The refraction reads the wallpaper through the terminal window, so it looks its best over an image and merely frosted over flat colour. Touch devices and reduced-motion users keep the blur and lose the displacement, which is the expensive half.

<sz-glass style="--glass-radius: 10px">
<div style="padding: 14px 16px">Anything can go under glass: this is a plain <code>div</code>.</div>
</sz-glass>

