Everything below is already running around this page, and a second instance would break the first. A second `sz-tmux-bar` re-binds `Alt`+`1`–`9`; a second `sz-palette` re-binds `:` `/` `?`; a second `sz-links` re-binds `l`. `sz-window` is `position: fixed`, so a copy would not sit in the prose column at all, and `sz-window-manager` binds document `mousemove`/`mouseup` to drive drags. So these are documented here and demonstrated by the page itself: run the trigger and watch the live instance.

No screenshots either. A screenshot of a component drifts the moment the component changes, silently, and no check can see it.

